    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3884" root="ترع" body-key="t">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ترّع البَابَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَتْرِيعٌ</span>, <i>He locked,</i> or <i>closed,
the door;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغْلَقَهُ</span> [which has both these significations]. (K.) In the Kur [xii. 23], some read,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَتَرَّعَتِ الأَبْوابَ</span> <i>And she locked,</i> or <i>closed, the
doors,</i> instead of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَلَّقَت</span>. (O, TA.)

